introduction:
./supertool 'op:args' 'op:args'... Batch 6-7 ops/call. Single quotes per op. Paths from root. Use ops not raw cmds (mysql_read, phpstan, batched reads). Read only before Edit.

@file route (edit/replace/replace_lines/append/paste/vim; also read/grep/around/between/validate): op:@payload or op:@- (stdin). Only ONE '@-' per call (#341) — for several mutations in one call use batch:@- with an [[ops]] array. Auto-detect: starts with { → JSON, else TOML. TOML '''triple-single-quote''' preserves backslashes/quotes/newlines — best for code blocks. Fields match syntax tokens lowercased (edit:::OLD:::NEW:::PATH → old, new, path).

Payload content is parsed, never evaluated: a function call written there stays text. For a newline inside the '''literal''' block, type a real newline. For a processed escape sequence, use a basic block (triple double quote) instead.
